{"id":"4047365","slug":"josh-jacobs","name":"Josh Jacobs","position":"RB","team":"GB","headshot":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/nfl/players/full/4047365.png","formats":{"ppr-12":{"positionRank":38,"ourRank":125,"vorRound":11,"adp":92.6,"projected":110.72,"vor":-37.44,"expectedGames":12.792920256940558,"floor":56.48593041151714,"median":110.65876022253583,"ceiling":164.83159003355453,"tier":6},"half-ppr-12":{"positionRank":37,"ourRank":123,"vorRound":11,"adp":84.8,"projected":104.35,"vor":-33.44,"expectedGames":12.792920256940558,"floor":52.58711291228321,"median":104.39022929663496,"ceiling":156.1933456809867,"tier":6},"standard-12":{"positionRank":40,"ourRank":134,"vorRound":12,"adp":77.7,"projected":83.96,"vor":-39.88000000000001,"expectedGames":12.792920256940558,"floor":39.58768393132194,"median":83.92155688553005,"ceiling":128.25542983973816,"tier":6}},"capsule":{"body":"The scoring profile is what sinks him. Our model grades his 35.4% touchdown-points share at -9.6 a game and his 20.9% red-zone touch share at -6.4, so the exact thing that made him RB13 last year is the thing we expect to cool off. He scored 15.8 a game in 2025 and finished above the weekly median in 12 of 15 weeks, but the regression factors all point down, and the expected 9.5 team wins cost him another 1.6 a game. Inside last season the snap share slid from 74% in weeks 1 to 4 down to 48% in weeks 14 to 17, so the workload was already trending the wrong way.\n\nThe availability picture does not help. We expect 13 games, with a range of 6 to 17, and he is already carrying an O designation as of October 13. The two prior seasons were healthy 17 and 15 game years, but 2023 he lost two weeks to injury, so the durability story has a dent in it. Age is a factor too, 28.6 on opening day in his eighth season.\n\nOur number is 111 points, RB38, and RBs drafted around pick 93 have historically gone for about 122.5 with the busts pooled in, so he is 11.8 points under that bar. Nine players sit in his tier before a 10.1-point cliff, which means his tier has room but he sits in it at ADP ahead of what we project. His ADP also slid 29.1 picks in late September, from 69.3 to 98.4, and drafters are clearly seeing the same things. Let him go at 93. If he falls past 120 or so, the RB13 talent is real enough to take a shot.","pulls":[{"figure":"111","caption":"projected PPR points"},{"figure":"93","caption":"his ADP in PPR drafts"}]},"season":{"season":2026,"format":"ppr-12","weeks":18,"through":5,"games":0,"pointsPerGame":null,"totals":{"pass_attempts":null,"completions":null,"passing_yards":null,"passing_touchdowns":null,"interceptions":null,"carries":null,"rushing_yards":null,"rushing_touchdowns":null,"targets":null,"receptions":null,"receiving_yards":null,"receiving_touchdowns":null,"fumbles_lost":null,"field_goals_made":null,"extra_points_made":null,"sacks":null,"defensive_interceptions":null,"defensive_touchdowns":null,"snapShare":null,"points":null},"log":[{"pass_attempts":null,"completions":null,"passing_yards":null,"passing_touchdowns":null,"interceptions":null,"carries":null,"rushing_yards":null,"rushing_touchdowns":null,"targets":null,"receptions":null,"receiving_yards":null,"receiving_touchdowns":null,"fumbles_lost":null,"field_goals_made":null,"extra_points_made":null,"sacks":null,"defensive_interceptions":null,"defensive_touchdowns":null,"snapShare":null,"points":null,"week":1,"opponent":"MIN","home":false,"status":"inactive"},{"pass_attempts":null,"completions":null,"passing_yards":null,"passing_touchdowns":null,"interceptions":null,"carries":null,"rushing_yards":null,"rushing_touchdowns":null,"targets":null,"receptions":null,"receiving_yards":null,"receiving_touchdowns":null,"fumbles_lost":null,"field_goals_made":null,"extra_points_made":null,"sacks":null,"defensive_interceptions":null,"defensive_touchdowns":null,"snapShare":null,"points":null,"week":2,"opponent":"NYJ","home":false,"status":"inactive"},{"pass_attempts":null,"completions":null,"passing